      `Buyers searching for ${ja("Flutter 開発")} (Flutter development) or React Native development usually want to know one thing: can one codebase really feel right on both platforms? For the kind of apps most businesses in Japan need, yes. Member cards, bookings, catalogues, ordering, checklists and forms are all well within what cross-platform frameworks handle, and the saving over two native apps is large.`,
      "<strong>Flutter</strong>, maintained by Google, renders its own widgets, so the interface looks identical on every device and custom designs, animations and brand-heavy screens are straightforward. It needs one extra detail for Japan: when an app does not declare Japanese as its locale, Flutter can fall back to Chinese glyph shapes for some kanji, because Chinese and Japanese share Unicode code points but draw certain characters differently. We set the locale and font fallbacks so Japanese users see the Japanese form of every character.",
