      `<strong>Points and prepaid balances.</strong> Point programmes are a normal part of Japanese retail, but a balance that customers buy with money in advance can count as a prepaid payment instrument under the Payment Services Act (${ja("資金決済法")}), while points given free as a bonus on purchases generally do not. If your app will sell prepaid value or let customers buy points, ask your adviser early, because the answer changes how the feature, the records and the refund rules should be designed.`,
